&style.oop;
public DateTimeDateTime::setDate intyear intmonth intday
&style.procedural;
DateTimedate_date_set DateTimeobject intyear intmonth intday
Resets the current date of the DateTime object to a different date.
Like DateTimeImmutable::setDate but works with DateTime, and changes the existing object.
The procedural version takes the DateTime object as its first argument.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.3.0

     A DateObjectError is now thrown for an
     object that has not been correctly initialized. Previously, an
     Error was thrown.

  &reftitle.examples;

   DateTime::setDate example
   &style.oop;


<?php
$date = new DateTime();
$date->setDate(2001, 2, 3);
echo $date->format('Y-m-d');


   &example.outputs;


2001-02-03


   &style.procedural;


<?php
$date = date_create();
date_date_set($date, 2001, 2, 3);
echo date_format($date, 'Y-m-d');


   &example.outputs;


2001-02-03




   Values exceeding ranges are added to their parent values


<?php
$date = new DateTime();

$date->setDate(2001, 2, 28);
echo $date->format('Y-m-d') . "\n";

$date->setDate(2001, 2, 29);
echo $date->format('Y-m-d') . "\n";

$date->setDate(2001, 14, 3);
echo $date->format('Y-m-d') . "\n";


   &example.outputs;


2001-02-28
2001-03-01
2002-02-03
